comment.narrative:
A baseline study will inform setting of the baseline value for the indicator. This study is part of the Contract for the development of the National Irrigation Strategy, which has started and is ongoing.&nbsp;

April 15, 2025
Research and data collection for this indicator is being carried out by the Statistics Agency. The main facilities in the Vakhshi Poyon subsystems are currently in the final stages of completion.

The 5 pumping stations modernized include: 3 pumping stations of the Norther Branch - Juybor canal network; and 2 pumping stations in the Subsystem L-2.&nbsp;

April 15, 2025
The 5 newly renovated pumping stations include:  (1) p/o Urtabuz, (2) p/o Urtabuz, (3) p/o Urtabuz in the Northern Branch Subsystem; and (4) p/o Bagara, and (5) p/o Tashurabad in the L-2 Sargah Subsystem.

The WIS javascript:;unit has been established and is staffed with the assigned specialists of TajikNigim (research institute under the MEWR) and external consultants currently financed by GIZ. No activities in support of WIS have been implemented under the project.&nbsp;

April 15, 2025
The National Water Information System (NWIS) team, comprising of 5 permanent staff, has been established. The detailed Terms of Reference are being finalized for submission to the bank by May 15, 2025. A list of necessary equipment to improve NWIS operations has been prepared and submitted for procurement, with installation expected by the end of Q4.

Consultations in the small-scale irrigation systems of upper catchments are finalized.&nbsp;

April 15, 2025
Consultations under Sub-component 2.2 of the Upper Vakhsh River Basin Project was conducted on a selection of small and medium-sized irrigation facilities, with a report submitted to the Bank in December 2023.
